<title>UK: LIFFE WHITE SUGAR ENDS BARELY DIFFERENT.</title>
<headline>LIFFE WHITE SUGAR ENDS BARELY DIFFERENT.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>White sugar futures ended little changed on Wednesday evening in thin activity.</p>
<p>Most-active October finished 20 cents firmer at $322.50 per tonne while December closed 40 cents easier at $319.30.</p>
<p>The bulk of the 1,740 lots turnover was in the front month, at 1,145 lots.</p>
<p>Trade buying at the lows helped support October, offsetting selling from other trade players and commission houses, traders said.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542-8065</p>
